Overlay patch, applied by build.sh after the pinned upstream commit is checked out.

What:    activation holds the measured pose instead of driving every joint to zero (OpenDubs arms
         plan A1, DEC-28). Two reads a refresh apart are checked (every motor answered, none in
         error, the reads agree within ~1 deg); a doubtful read refuses with the motors still
         disabled. Then the pose is held while the stiffness ramps from zero over 0.5 s, and
         pos_commands_ is seeded with it, because write() would otherwise command zero before any
         controller writes. The checks and the ramp are pure, in activation_hold.hpp, with a unit
         test that needs no ROS.
Against: enactic/openarm_ros2 c15982d910eb3c09f03ed4b7ac7ae737427a1397 (what opendubs2 runs,
         per capture-pins.sh, 2026-10-09).
Author:  the project team. Apache-2.0, as the upstream repository.
Status:  to be offered to enactic upstream. Delete this file when upstream has it.

