+// Activation holds the arm where it is (OpenDubs arms plan A1) instead of return_to_zero(), which
+// swept every joint to 0 rad. Read the pose twice, refuse a doubtful read with the motors still
+// disabled, then hold exactly that pose while the stiffness ramps up from zero. pos_commands_ is
+// seeded with the same pose, because write() sends it every cycle from now on -- before any
+// controller has written a target, it would otherwise still command zero.
